FAILURES: none.

OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking):
- The `.num` span used for "Spending versus plan" tile's figure
  (`<span class="num">$18,965.19</span> under`) reports `scrollWidth`/
  `clientWidth` of 0/0 when queried directly, because it is an inline
  element (clientWidth/scrollWidth are spec'd as 0 for non-replaced inline
  elements). This is pre-existing structural behavior unrelated to RF2's
  size bump; verified no overflow instead via the parent `<p>` element,
  which is block and shows `scrollWidth == clientWidth` at both viewports.
  Checkers auditing future `.num` reflow claims should query the parent
  block element, not the inline span itself.
- All contrast ratios measured (5.21:1 to 16.03:1) are far above their
  floors; no near-miss values worth flagging for RF1's future palette
  tuning.
